    2. Choose number of objects N in 1-4
    3. For each object, pick 2 distinct non-bg colors and a split (minority_count in 2-4)
    4. Fill a 3x3 patch randomly with the two colors matching the chosen split
    5. Place objects on the grid with >=1 border padding and >=2 L-inf separation between all pairs
    6. Output is obtained by swapping the two colors within each object
